# Version pins for incus-compose-update. Image refs in compose.yaml
# interpolate these; check/apply reads and writes them. Tracked in git.
# Secrets stay in .env (gitignored).
#
# Pin targets verified 2026-08-26.

# Buzz relay. NO SEMVER TAGS EXIST for this image — verified against the
# registry on 2026-08-26: `v0.5.2`, `0.5.2` and `v0.4.26` all 404, and every
# GitHub release since 2026-07-31 is `desktop-v0.5.x` (the Tauri app), which
# publishes no relay image. What the registry actually carries is `main`,
# `latest`, and several hundred `sha-<7>` per-commit builds.
#
# Do NOT reach for a `sha256-<hex>` tag: those are Sigstore attestation bundles
# (SLSA provenance), not images. `main`'s digest reads `sha256:<hex>` and the
# tag `sha256-<same-hex>` is its signature, which makes them easy to confuse.
# The runnable per-commit tag is `sha-<7>` — one dash, seven hex characters.
#
# Do NOT reach for `:latest` — it is stale (built 2026-08-08) and carries a
# misleading `org.opencontainers.image.version=0.2.1` label while upstream's
# release line reads v0.5.x. It is not an alias for `main`; the digests differ.
#
# sha-822c5ab == :main as of 2026-08-26 (both sha256:7bda3a2e3505f613...).
# The 7-hex suffix is the upstream commit, so you can read the diff before
# applying an update: https://github.com/block/buzz/compare/822c5ab...<new>
BUZZ_TAG=sha-822c5ab

# Postgres — upstream's bundle pins 17-alpine. tag_re allows 17-19 so the
# updater surfaces a major bump as a candidate rather than hiding it, but a
# major Postgres upgrade needs a dump/restore, not just a pin change.
POSTGRES_TAG=17-alpine

# Redis — upstream pins the 7 line.
REDIS_TAG=7-alpine

# MinIO and its client. Literal pins copied from upstream's bundle: these are
# the versions Buzz is tested against, so they move when upstream moves, not
# when the registry does. No x-update block for either.
MINIO_TAG=RELEASE.2025-09-07T16-13-09Z
MINIO_MC_TAG=RELEASE.2025-08-13T08-35-41Z
